# `join t key`: only `on` is missing, so the fix inserts it.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..52
  PIPELINE@0..51
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    JOIN_OP@20..51
      IDENT@20..24 "join"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      LITERAL@25..40
        STRING@25..40 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
      NAME_REF@41..51
        IDENT@41..51 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@51..52 "\n"

error[DS0122]: `join` needs `on` and the columns to match
  --> query:1:42
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' customerId
  |                                          ^^^^^^^^^^ expected `on` before this
  |
  = help: insert `on`: `join 'customers.csv' on customerId`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
